un the command once immediately on startup. character(len=:), public, allocatable :: self_exe Explicit supervisor child executable, otherwise resolved from argv/environment. logical, public :: silent_fpm = .false. Suppress both command output streams; watcher and model records remain separate. integer, public :: verbosity = 0 Verbosity level: -1 : quiet (errors and enabled output protocol) 0 : normal 1..2 : more detail logical, public :: watch_deps = .false. Also watch dependency project sources (can include paths under build dir). Source Code type watch_opts_t !> Verbosity level: !! !! - `-1`: quiet (errors and enabled output protocol) !! - `0`: normal !! - `1..2`: more detail integer :: verbosity = 0 !> Output format: text (default), json (JSON Lines), or logfmt. character ( len = :), allocatable :: log_format !> Executable used for build/test/run; defaults to `fpm` on PATH. character ( len = :), allocatable :: fpm_executable !> Enable debug-level records; quiet mode still suppresses them. logical :: debug = . false . !> Seconds between polling scans; normalized to at least 0.05. real :: poll = 0.5 !> Seconds to wait after detecting a change before resampling. real :: debounce = 0.2 !> Optional periodic rescan interval (seconds). `0` disables periodic rescans. real :: rescan = 0.0 !> Run the command once immediately on startup. logical :: run_on_start = . true . !> Request a startup file list; the logger additionally requires verbosity 2. logical :: print_files_once = . false . !> Suppress both command output streams; watcher and model records remain separate. logical :: silent_fpm = . false . !> Bracket command stderr and force cycle events in structured logging only. logical :: output_markers = . false . !> Internal supervisor generation, retained during manifest refresh. integer :: restart_count = 0 !> Also watch dependency project sources (can include paths under build dir). logical :: watch_deps = . false . !> Ignore globs, applied after include rules; manifest/version metadata bypass filtering. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: ignore (:) !> Include globs; empty means all eligible files. Manifest/version metadata always remain. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: include (:) !> Run once (init + optional run-on-start) and exit (CI-friendly). logical :: once = . false . !> Restart failed watcher children until success or the configured limit. logical :: auto_restart = . false . !> Internal child marker preventing recursive supervision. logical :: is_child = . false . !> Seconds between failed child exits and the next launch. real :: restart_delay = 1.0 !> Maximum restarts after initial launch; zero means unlimited. integer :: restart_max = 0 !> Explicit supervisor child executable, otherwise resolved from argv/environment. character ( len = :), allocatable :: self_exe end type watch_opts_t","tags":"","url":"type/watch_opts_t.html"},{"title":"watch_snapshot_t – fpm-watch ","text":"type, public :: watch_snapshot_t One aligned watch-list snapshot, including membership and change baselines. Inherits type~~watch_snapshot_t~~InheritsGraph type~watch_snapshot_t watch_snapshot_t string_t string_t type~watch_snapshot_t->string_t files type~root_info_t root_info_t type~watch_snapshot_t->type~root_info_t roots Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Inherited by type~~watch_snapshot_t~~InheritedByGraph type~watch_snapshot_t watch_snapshot_t type~watcher_t watcher_t type~watcher_t->type~watch_snapshot_t snapshot Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entit