len ( encoded ), 2 ) /= 0 ) return deallocate ( decoded ) allocate ( character ( len = len ( encoded ) / 2 ) :: decoded ) do i = 1 , len ( decoded ) high = index ( digits , encoded ( 2 * i - 1 : 2 * i - 1 )) - 1 low = index ( digits , encoded ( 2 * i : 2 * i )) - 1 if ( high < 0 . or . low < 0 ) return byte = 16 * high + low if ( byte == 0 ) return decoded ( i : i ) = achar ( byte ) end do valid = . true . end subroutine decode_bytes","tags":"","url":"proc/decode_bytes.html"},{"title":"invalid_response – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine invalid_response(error, detail) Report malformed worker data without accepting a partial snapshot. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(error_t), intent(out), allocatable :: error character(len=*), intent(in) :: detail Calls proc~~invalid_response~~CallsGraph proc~invalid_response invalid_response fatal_error fatal_error proc~invalid_response->fatal_error Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~invalid_response~~CalledByGraph proc~invalid_response invalid_response proc~read_graph_response read_graph_response proc~read_graph_response->proc~invalid_response proc~compute_watch_snapshot compute_watch_snapshot proc~compute_watch_snapshot->proc~read_graph_response proc~rebuild_watch_list rebuild_watch_list proc~rebuild_watch_list->proc~compute_watch_snapshot proc~handle_m