le n = n + 1 paths ( n ) = files ( idx ) end do call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.changed\" , message , & [ log_int ( \"file_count\" , changed_count ), log_strings ( \"paths\" , paths (: n )), & log_real ( \"debounce_ms\" , w % debounce * 100 0.0 )]) else call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.changed\" , message ) end if do i = 1 , min ( changed_count , 8 ) idx = changed_idx ( i ) if ( idx < 1 . or . idx > size ( files )) cycle call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.changed_file\" , \"Changed \" // files ( idx )% s , & [ log_string ( \"path\" , files ( idx )% s )], verbosity = 1 ) end do end subroutine report_changes","tags":"","url":"proc/report_changes.html"},{"title":"run_command_and_report – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine run_command_and_report(cmd, w, exitstat, secs) Execute synchronously and report start, completion, exit status, and seconds. cycle_id combines the supervisor generation and a process-local counter.\nStructured mode sends raw command stdout to stderr; silent mode suppresses\nboth child streams. In structured mode only, output markers bracket stderr\nand force both command events through quiet filtering. Failures are errors;\na latched user interruption is reported as an interrupted completion. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: cmd Complete serialized command to execute synchronously. type( watch_opts_t ), intent(in) :: w Output suppression, cycle generation, and optional output-marker settings. integer, intent(out) :: exitstat Command status, including 127 when the platform wrapper cannot launch or wait. real, intent(out) :: secs Elapsed command time in seconds, excluding event formatting and boundary writes. Calls proc~~run_command_and_report~~CallsGraph proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report interface~log_int log_int proc~run_command_and_report->interface~log_int proc~execute_command execute_command proc~run_command_and_report->proc~execute_command proc~ftoa ftoa proc~run_command_and