module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine apply_watch_from_manifest ( w , manifest ) type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: manifest type ( toml_table ), allocatable :: root type ( toml_table ), pointer :: wt logical :: ok call load_watch_table ( root , wt , ok , manifest ) if (. not . ok ) return call toml_get_real ( wt , \"poll\" , w % poll ) call toml_get_real ( wt , \"debounce\" , w % debounce ) call toml_get_real ( wt , \"rescan\" , w % rescan ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"debug\" , w % debug ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"print-files\" , w % print_files_once ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"silent-fpm\" , w % silent_fpm ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"output-markers\" , w % output_markers ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"run-on-start\" , w % run_on_start ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"deps\" , w % watch_deps ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"once\" , w % once ) call toml_get_int ( wt , \"verbosity\" , w % verbosity ) call toml_get_string ( wt , \"log-format\" , w % log_format ) call toml_get_string ( wt , \"fpm-executable\" , w % fpm_executable ) call toml_get_list_strings ( wt , \"ignore\" , w % ignore ) call toml_get_list_strings ( wt , \"include\" , w % include ) call toml_get_logical ( wt , \"auto-restart\" , w % auto_restart ) call toml_get_real ( wt , \"restart-delay\" , w % restart_delay ) call toml_get_int ( wt , \"restart-max\" , w % restart_max ) call toml_get_string ( wt , \"self\" , w % self_exe ) call normalize_watch_opts ( w ) end subroutine apply_watch_from_manifest","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_watch_from_manifest.html"},{"title":"normalize_watch_opts – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine normalize_watch_opts(w) Normalize timing bounds, verbosity, and the executable name. Clamp poll to at least 0.05 s, debounce/rescan to nonnegative values, and\nverbosity to -1..2. Restore an empty/unallocated fpm executable to fpm .\nLog-format validation and list allocation are handled separately. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( watch_opts_t ), intent(inout) :: w Called by proc~~normalize_watch_opts~~CalledByGraph proc~normalize_watch_opts normalize_watch_opts proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~normalize_watch_opts proc~apply_watch_from_manifest apply_watch_from_manifest proc~apply_watch_from_manifest->proc~normalize_watch_opts proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~normalize_watch_opts proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_from_manifest proc~apply_watch_arguments apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~parse_cli_config->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine normalize_watch_opts ( w ) type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w if ( w % poll < 0.05 ) w % poll = 0.05 if ( w % debounce < 0.0 ) w % debounce = 0.0 if ( w % rescan < 0.0 ) w % rescan = 0.0 if ( w % restart_delay < 0.0 ) w % restart_delay = 0.0 if ( w % restart_max < 0 ) w % restart_max = 0 if ( w % verbosity > 2 ) w % verbosity = 2 if ( w % verbosity < - 1 ) w % verbosity = - 1 if (. not . allocated ( w % fpm_executable )) w % fpm_executable = \"fpm\" if ( len_trim ( w % fpm_executable ) == 0 ) w % fpm_executable = \"fpm\" end subroutine normalize_watch_opts","tags":"","url":"proc/normalize_watch_opts.html"},{"title":"push_feature – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine push_feature(features, name) Append a unique, nonempty, right-trimmed string to an allocatable list. Used for fpm features, target patterns, and filters.\nComparisons are case-sensitive; leading whitespace is retained. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(string_t), intent(inout), allocatable :: features (:) character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Called by proc~~push_feature~~CalledByGraph proc~push_feature push_feature proc~add_features_csv add_features_csv proc~add_features_csv->proc~push_feature proc~add_target_names add_target_names proc~add_target_names->proc~push_feature proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~push_feature proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~push_feature proc~parse_cli->proc~add_features_csv proc~parse_cli->proc~add_target_names proc~read_response_options read_response_options proc~parse_cli->proc~read_response_options proc~apply_watch_arguments apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~prepare_response_options prepare_response_options proc~prepare_response_options->proc~push_feature proc~response_candidates response_candidates proc~prepare_response_options->proc~response_candidates proc~read_response_options->proc~push_feature proc~read_response_options->proc~add_features_csv proc~read_response_options->proc~add_target_names proc~response_candidates->proc~push_feature proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~parse_cli_config->proc~prepare_response_options proc~parse_cli_config->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine push_feature ( features , name ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: features (:) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name integer :: n , i type ( string_t ), allocatable :: tmp (:) if ( len_trim ( name ) == 0 ) return if (. not . allocated ( features )) then allocate ( features ( 1 )) features ( 1 )% s = trim ( name ) return end if do i = 1 , size ( features ) if ( trim ( features ( i )% s ) == trim ( name )) return end do n = size ( features ) allocate ( tmp ( n + 1 )) tmp ( 1 : n ) = features tmp ( n + 1 )% s = trim ( name ) call move_alloc ( tmp , features ) end subroutine push_feature","tags":"","url":"proc/push_feature.html"},{"title":"set_watch_defaults – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine set_watch_defaults(w) Reset scalar watcher options and ensure list arrays are allocated. Existing include/ignore arrays are retained. Fresh options receive empty arrays. Arguments Type Intent Op