ric interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine configure_logging ( w ) type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( in ) :: w active_format = \"text\" if ( allocated ( w % log_format )) active_format = w % log_format active_verbosity = w % verbosity active_debug = w % debug end subroutine configure_logging","tags":"","url":"proc/configure_logging.html"},{"title":"log_event – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine log_event(level, event, message, fields, verbosity, force) Format, write, and flush one timestamped event with optional typed attributes. verbosity is the minimum detail level, defaulting to zero. Quiet mode\nsuppresses non-error records; debug records additionally require debug mode. force=true and errors bypass both filters. Structured output always uses\nstdout; only text errors use stderr. fields should use the typed constructors.\nOutput errors are nonfatal so a disconnected terminal cannot replace a\ncommand or cancellation status with a Fortran runtime I/O failure. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: level Severity, stable event identifier, and human-readable message, respectively. character(len=*), intent(in) :: event Severity, stable event identifier, and human-readable message, respectively. character(len=*), intent(in) :: message Severity, stable event identifier, and human-readable message, respectively. type( log_field_t ), intent(in), optional :: fields (:) Typed attributes constructed with log_string/log_strings/log_int/log_real/log_bool. integer, intent(in), optional :: verbosity Minimum active verbosity for this non-error event; defaults to zero. logical, intent(in), optional :: force Bypass verbosity/debug filters for required protocol events; defaults to false. Calls proc~~log_event~~CallsGraph proc~log_event log_event proc~form