ch it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine release_targets ( targets ) type ( build_target_ptr ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: targets (:) integer :: i if (. not . allocated ( targets )) return do i = 1 , size ( targets ) if ( associated ( targets ( i )% ptr )) deallocate ( targets ( i )% ptr ) end do deallocate ( targets ) end subroutine release_targets","tags":"","url":"proc/release_targets.html"},{"title":"select_names_or_all – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine select_names_or_all(targets, scope, names, keep) Mark executable targets in scope matching names without clearing existing marks. Absent/empty name patterns select all executables in scope. Otherwise match\nfpm globs against each output basename with and without its suffix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(build_target_ptr), intent(in) :: targets (:) integer, intent(in) :: scope character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: names (:) logical, intent(inout) :: keep (:) Calls proc~~select_names_or_all~~CallsGraph proc~select_names_or_all select_names_or_all basename basename proc~select_names_or_all->basename glob glob proc~select_names_or_all->glob proc~is_program_in_scope is_program_in_scope proc~select_names_or_all->proc~is_program_in_scope Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that in