erface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine supervisor_loop ( delay0 , max0 , exe0 , log_format ) real , intent ( in ) :: delay0 integer , intent ( in ) :: max0 character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: exe0 character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: log_format character ( len = :), allocatable :: child_cmd integer :: code , attempt real :: delay logical :: interrupted attempt = 0 delay = max ( 0.0 , delay0 ) do code = 0 child_cmd = build_child_command ( exe0 , log_format , attempt ) call execute_supervised_child ( child_cmd , code , interrupted ) if ( interrupted ) then call log_event ( \"info\" , \"supervisor.stopped\" , \"Supervisor interrupted\" , [ log_string ( \"reason\" , \"interrupt\" )]) stop code , quiet = . true . end if if ( code == 0 ) exit if ( max0 > 0 . and . attempt >= max0 ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"supervisor.limit_reached\" , \"Child failed; restart limit reached\" , & [ log_int ( \"exit_code\" , code ), log_int ( \"restart_count\" , attempt )]) stop code , quiet = . true . end if attempt = attempt + 1 call log_event ( \"warn\" , \"supervisor.restart\" , & \"Child failed (exit \" // str ( code ) // \"); restart #\" // str ( attempt ) // \" in \" // ftoa ( delay ) // \"s\" , & [ log_int ( \"exit_code\" , code ), log_int ( \"restart_count\" , attempt ), log_real ( \"delay_ms\" , delay * 100 0.0 )]) call sleep_seconds ( delay ) end do stop 0 end subroutine supervisor_loop","tags":"","url":"proc/supervisor_loop.html"},{"title":"any_configuration_changed – fpm-watch","text":"private  function any_configuration_changed(files, changed_idx, changed_count, response_files) result(hit) Return whether changed manifests or response candidates require reparsing settings. Manifest detection uses the basename and therefore triggers if any\nwatched fpm.toml changes (main or dependency manifests).\nResponse paths are absolute candidates supplied by the CLI adapter. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: files (:) integer, intent(in) :: changed_idx (:) integer, intent(in) :: changed_count type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: response_files (:) Return Value logical Calls proc~~any_configuration_changed~~CallsGraph proc~any_configuration_changed any_configuration_changed basename basename proc~any_configuration_changed->basename Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~any_configuration_changed~~CalledByGraph proc~any_configuration_changed any_configuration_changed proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~any_configuration_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code logical function any_configuration_changed ( files , changed_idx , changed_count , response_files ) result ( hit ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: files (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: changed_idx (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: changed_count type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: response_files (:) integer :: j , idx , k character ( len = :), allocatable :: b hit = . false . if (. not . allocated ( files )) return do j = 1 , changed_count idx = changed_idx ( j ) if ( idx < 1 . or . idx > size ( files )) cycle b = basename ( files ( idx )% s ) if ( b == \"fpm.toml\" ) then hit = . true . return end if if (. not . allocated ( response_files )) cycle do k = 1 , size ( response_files ) if ( files ( idx )% s /= response_files ( k )% s ) cycle hit = . true . return end do end do end function any_configuration_changed","tags":"","url":"proc/any_configuration_changed.html"},{"title":"root_mapping_changed – fpm-watch","text":"private pure function root_mapping_changed(old_roots, new_roots) result(changed) Return whether root names or their bits changed during a dependency refresh. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( root_info_t ), intent(in), allocatable :: old_roots (:) type( root_info_t ), intent(in), allocatable :: new_roots (:) Return Value logical Called by proc~~root_mapping_changed~~CalledByGraph proc~root_mapping_changed root_mapping_changed proc~rebuild_watch_list rebuild_watch_list proc~rebuild_watch_list->proc~root_mapping_changed proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_