ogram This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine apply_watch_arguments ( w , first_arg , subcmd_pos , log_format ) type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w integer , intent ( in ) :: first_arg integer , intent ( out ) :: subcmd_pos character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: log_format character ( len = :), allocatable :: arg integer :: narg , i if ( present ( log_format )) w % log_format = log_format if ( valid_log_format ( w % log_format )) call configure_logging ( w ) narg = command_argument_count () if ( narg < first_arg ) call usage_and_stop ( \"missing fpm subcommand (build/test/run)\" ) i = first_arg do while ( i <= narg ) arg = get_arg ( i ) if ( is_watch_flag ( arg )) then call apply_watch_flag ( arg , i , narg , w ) else if ( arg == \"-q\" ) then w % verbosity = - 1 else if ( arg == \"-v\" ) then w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , 1 ) else if ( arg == \"-vv\" ) then w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , 2 ) else exit end if i = i + 1 end do if ( present ( log_format )) w % log_format = log_format if (. not . valid_log_format ( w % log_format )) then call usage_and_stop ( \"invalid log-format: \" // w % log_format // \"; use text, json, or logfmt\" ) end if call configure_logging ( w ) if ( i > narg ) call usage_and_stop ( \"missing fpm subcommand (build/test/run)\" ) arg = get_arg ( i ) if ( arg == \"--help\" . or . arg == \"-h\" ) call usage_and_stop_ok () subcmd_pos = i end subroutine apply_watch_arguments","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_watch_arguments.html"},{"title":"apply_watch_flag – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine apply_watch_flag(a, i, narg, w) Consume one leading watcher flag and normalize its options. Required value options accept =value or advance i to the next token.\nBoolean and verbosity values use =value ; bare boolean flags enable the\nsetting. Numeric parse failures retain a fallback value. Supervisor flags\nare consumed here but applied separately by watch_restart . Unknown flags\nor invalid log formats exit with status 2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(inout) :: i integer, intent(in) :: narg type( watch_opts_t ), intent(inout) :: w Calls proc~~apply_watch_flag~~CallsGraph proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~configure_logging configure_logging proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~configure_logging proc~get_arg get_arg proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~get_arg proc~normalize_watch_opts normalize_watch_opts proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~normalize_watch_opts proc~parse_bool parse_bool proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~parse_bool proc~parse_int parse_int proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~parse_int proc~parse_real parse_real proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~parse_real proc~push_feature push_feature proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~push_feature proc~usage_and_stop usage_and_stop proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~usage_and_stop proc~usage_and_stop_ok usage_and_stop_ok proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~usage_and_stop_ok proc~valid_log_format valid_log_format proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~valid_log_format proc~watch_option_takes_value watch_option_takes_value proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~watch_option_takes_value proc~lower_ascii lower_ascii proc~parse_bool->proc~lower_ascii proc~log_event log_event proc~usage_and_stop->proc~log_event proc~structured_logging structured_logging proc~usage_and_stop->proc~structured_logging proc~usage_print_only usage_print_only proc~usage_and_stop_ok->proc~usage_print_only proc~format_log_record format_log_record proc~log_event->proc~format_log_record proc~log_timestamp log_timestamp proc~log_event->proc~log_timestamp proc~escape_text escape_text proc~format_log_record->proc~escape_text proc~escaped_length escaped_length proc~format_log_record->proc~escaped_length proc~json_quote json_quote proc~format_log_record->proc~json_quote proc~put_json_string put_json_string proc~format_log_record->proc~put_json_string proc~put_text put_text proc~format_log_record->proc~put_text proc~escape_text->proc~escaped_length proc~put_escaped put_escaped proc~escape_text->proc~put_escaped proc~escape_piece escape_piece proc~escaped_length->proc~escape_piece proc~json_quote->proc~escaped_length proc~json_quote->proc~put_json_string proc~put_json_string->proc~put_text proc~put_json_string->proc~put_escaped proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~escape_piece->proc~utf8_width proc~put_escaped->proc~put_text proc~put_escaped->proc~escape_piece Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~apply_watch_flag~~CalledByGraph proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_arguments apply_watch_arguments proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine apply_watch_flag ( a , i , narg , w ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: a integer , intent ( inout ) :: i integer , intent ( in ) :: narg type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w character ( len = :), allocatable :: key , val integer :: eq key = trim ( a ) val = \"\" eq = index ( key , \"=\" ) if ( eq > 0 ) then val = key ( eq + 1 :) key = key ( 1 : eq - 1 ) else if ( watch_option_takes_value ( a )) then if ( i >= narg ) call usage_and_stop ( key // \" requires a value\" ) i = i + 1 val = get_arg ( i ) end if select case ( key ) case ( \"--watch-child\" ) w % is_child = . true . w % restart_count = max ( 0 , parse_int ( val , 0 )) case ( \"--watch-auto-restart\" ) w % auto_restart = parse_bool ( val , . true .) case ( \"--watch-restart-delay\" ) w % restart_delay = parse_real ( val , w % restart_delay ) case ( \"--watch-restart-max\" ) w % restart_max = parse_int ( val , w % restart_max ) case ( \"--watch-self\" ) w % self_exe = val case ( \"--watch-fpm\" ) if ( len_trim ( val ) == 0 ) call usage_and_stop ( \"--watch-fpm requires an executable path or name\" ) w % fpm_executable = val case ( \"--watch-deps\" ) if ( len_trim ( val ) > 0 ) then w % watch_deps = parse_bool ( val , . true .) else w % watch_deps = . true . end if case ( \"--watch-no-deps\" ) w % watch_deps = . false . case ( \"--watch-quiet\" ) w % verbosity = - 1 case ( \"--watch-log-format\" ) if (. not . valid_log_format ( val )) call usage_and_stop ( \"--watch-log-format requires text, json, or logfmt\" ) w % log_format = val call configure_logging ( w ) case ( \"--watch-verbose\" ) if ( len_trim ( val ) > 0 ) then w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , parse_int ( val , 1 )) else w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , 1 ) end if case ( \"--watch-very-verbose\" ) w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , 2 ) case ( \"--watch-debug\" ) w % debug = parse_bool ( val , . true .) case ( \"--watch-print-files\" ) w % print_files_once = parse_bool ( val , . true .) if ( w % print_files_once ) w % verbosity = max ( w % verbosity , 2 ) case ( \"--watch-silent-fpm\" ) w % silent_fpm = parse_bool ( val , . true .) case ( \"--watch-output-markers\" ) w % output_markers = parse_bool ( val , . true .) case ( \"--watch-run-on-start\" ) w % run_on_start = . true . case ( \"--watch-no-run-on-start\" ) w % run_on_start = . false . case ( \"--watch-rescan\" ) w % rescan = parse_real ( val , w % rescan ) case ( \"--watch-no-rescan\" ) w % rescan = 0.0 case ( \"--watch-ignore\" ) call push_feature ( w % ignore , trim ( val )) case ( \"--watch-include\" ) call push_feature ( w % include , trim ( val )) case ( \"--watch-poll\" ) w % poll = parse_real ( val , w % poll ) case ( \"--watch-debounce\" ) w % debounce = parse_real ( val , w % debounce ) case ( \"--watch-once\" ) if ( len_trim ( val ) > 0 ) then w % once = parse_bool ( val , . true .) else w % once = . true . end if case ( \"--watch-help\" ) call usage_and_stop_ok () case default call usage_and_stop ( \"unknown watch flag: \" // trim ( a )) end select call normalize_watch_opts ( w ) end subroutine apply_watch_flag","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_watch_flag.html"},{"title":"init_build_settings – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine init_build_settings(settings, build_dir, prune, profile, features, compiler_in, c_compiler_in, cxx_compiler_in, archiver_in, flag_in, cflag_in, cxxflag_in, ldflag_in) Copy parsed build and toolchain values into a typed fpm settings object. parse_cli resolves environment defaults and CLI overrides beforehand.\nThis routine disables model verbosity, replaces the feature array, and\nassigns toolchain/flag strings. An empty profile retains the type default. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(fpm_build_settings), intent(inout) :: settings character(len=*), intent(in) :: build_dir logical, intent(in) :: prune character(len=*), intent(in) :: profile type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: features (:) character(len=*), intent(in) :: compiler_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: c_compiler_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: cxx_compiler_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: archiver_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: flag_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: cflag_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: cxxflag_in character(len=*), intent(in) :: ldflag_in Calls proc~~init_build_settings~~CallsGraph proc~init_build_settings init_build_settings features features proc~init_build_settings->features Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~init_build_settings~~CalledByGraph proc~init_build_settings init_build_settings proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~init