s Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~read_response_options~~CalledByGraph proc~read_response_options read_response_options proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~read_response_options proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine read_response_options ( profile , build_dir , compiler , c_compiler , cxx_compiler , archiver , & flag , cflag , cxxflag , ldflag , runner , runner_args , config_file , features , names , prune , example , build_tests , & subcmd , original_subcmd ) character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: profile , build_dir , compiler , c_compiler , cxx_compiler , archiver character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: flag , cflag , cxxflag , ldflag , runner , runner_args , config_file type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: features (:), names (:) logical , intent ( inout ) :: prune , example , build_tests character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: subcmd , original_subcmd integer :: i , first_name if ( specified ( \"profile\" )) profile = sget ( \"profile\" ) if ( specified ( \"features\" )) call add_features_csv ( features , sget ( \"features\" )) if ( specified ( \"build-dir\" )) build_dir = sget ( \"build-dir\" ) if ( specified ( \"compiler\" )) compiler = sget ( \"compiler\" ) if ( specified ( \"c-compiler\" )) c_compiler = sget ( \"c-compiler\" ) if ( specified ( \"cxx-compiler\" )) cxx_compiler = sget ( \"cxx-compiler\" ) if ( specified ( \"archiver\" )) archiver = sget ( \"archiver\" ) if ( specified ( \"flag\" )) flag = sget ( \"flag\" ) if ( specified ( \"c-flag\" )) cflag = sget ( \"c-flag\" ) if ( specified ( \"cxx-flag\" )) cxxflag = sget ( \"cxx-flag\" ) if ( specified ( \"link-flag\" )) ldflag = sget ( \"link-flag\" ) if ( specified ( \"runner\" )) runner = sget ( \"runner\" ) if ( specified ( \"runner-args\" )) runner_args = sget ( \"runner-args\" ) if ( specified ( \"config-file\" )) config_file = sget ( \"config-file\" ) if ( specified ( \"no-prune\" )) prune = . not . lget ( \"no-prune\" ) if ( specified ( \"prune\" )) prune = lget ( \"prune\" ) example = lget ( \"example\" ) build_tests = lget ( \"tests\" ) if ( specified ( \"target\" )) call add_target_names ( names , sget ( \"target\" )) if ( lget ( \"all\" )) call push_feature ( names , \"*\" ) first_name = 1 do i = 1 , size ( unnamed ) if ( trim ( unnamed ( i )) /= original_subcmd ) cycle first_name = i + 1 exit end do if ( subcmd /= \"run\" . and . subcmd /= \"test\" ) return do i = first_name , size ( unnamed ) call push_feature ( names , target_pattern ( trim ( unnamed ( i )))) end do end subroutine read_response_options","tags":"","url":"proc/read_response_options.html"},{"title":"response_candidates – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine response_candidates(argument, candidates, error) Enumerate documented named-file locations without interpreting option values. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: argument type(string_t), intent(out), allocatable :: candidates (:) type(error_t), intent(out), allocatable :: error Calls proc~~response_candidates~~CallsGraph proc~response_candidates response_candidates canon_path canon_path proc~response_candidates->canon_path fatal_error fatal_error proc~response_candidates->fatal_error get_current_directory get_current_directory proc~response_candidates->get_current_directory get_env get_env proc~response_candidates->get_env is_absolute_path is_absolute_path proc~response_candidates->is_absolute_path join_path join_path proc~response_candidates->join_path proc~push_feature push_feature proc~response_candidates->proc~push_feature split split proc~response_candidates->split Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~response_candidates~~CalledByGraph proc~response_candidates response_candidates proc~prepare_response_options prepare_response_options proc~prepare_response_options->proc~response_candidates proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~prepare_response_options proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_cha