har ( 0 ) // \",:\" ) do i = 1 , size ( paths ) candidate = paths ( i ) if (. not . is_absolute_path ( candidate )) candidate = join_path ( base , candidate ) call push_feature ( candidates , canon_path ( join_path ( candidate , name ))) end do end subroutine response_candidates","tags":"","url":"proc/response_candidates.html"},{"title":"set_names – fpm-watch","text":"private pure subroutine set_names(s, names) Copy nonempty target patterns into an initially unallocated s%name . Patterns come from positional names, --target , or --all . Empty or\nunallocated input leaves s%name unchanged; copied names are right-trimmed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(fpm_run_settings), intent(inout) :: s type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: names (:) Calls proc~~set_names~~CallsGraph proc~set_names set_names name name proc~set_names->name Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~set_names~~CalledByGraph proc~set_names set_names proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~set_names proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: G