n interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~usage_and_stop_ok~~CalledByGraph proc~usage_and_stop_ok usage_and_stop_ok proc~apply_watch_arguments apply_watch_arguments proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~usage_and_stop_ok proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~usage_and_stop_ok proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine usage_and_stop_ok () call usage_print_only () stop 0 end subroutine usage_and_stop_ok","tags":"","url":"proc/usage_and_stop_ok.html"},{"title":"usage_print_only – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine usage_print_only() Print the fpm-watch help text. The help includes:\n- Watcher options ( --watch-* ),\n- Project configuration ( [extra.fpm-watch] ),\n- Examples and behavioral notes. Arguments None Called by proc~~usage_print_only~~CalledByGraph proc~usage_print_only usage_print_only proc~usage_and_stop_ok usage_and_stop_ok proc~usage_and_stop_ok->proc~usage_print_only proc~apply_watch_arguments apply_watch_arguments proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~usage_and_stop_ok proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_arguments->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~usage_and_stop_ok proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~apply_watch_arguments proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine usage_print_only () write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"fpm-watch — Smart file watcher plugin for fpm projects\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"USAGE\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch [watch options] <build|test|run> [fpm options]\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  Everything after <build|test|run> is passed to fpm unchanged.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"WATCH OPTIONS\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-help\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Show this help and exit.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-quiet | -q\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Quiet mode (errors only).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-log-format <text|json|logfmt>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Log format (default: text). Structured logs use stdout; fpm output uses stderr.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-verbose[=N] | -v\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Increase verbosity. N: 0..2 (default: 1).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-very-verbose | -vv\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Same as verbosity=2 (prints watch list, more details).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-debug\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Extra debug logs. Use --watch-debug=false to disable a manifest setting.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-deps\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Also watch dependency source trees (including deps under build/).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-no-deps\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Disable dependency watching (default).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-poll <sec>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Poll interval for file checks. Default: 0.5\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-debounce <sec>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Wait after first change to coalesce edits. Default: 0.2\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-rescan <sec>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Rebuild the fpm model periodically (slow on big projects). Default: 0 (off).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-no-rescan\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Disable periodic rebuild (recommended).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-run-on-start\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Run the command once immediately on startup. Default: on.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-no-run-on-start\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Only run after a change is detected.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-silent-fpm\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Suppress fpm output; keep only fpm-watch status lines.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Use --watch-silent-fpm=false to override manifest suppression.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-fpm <path>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      fpm executable to invoke (default: fpm on PATH).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-output-markers\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Frame raw stderr with cycle markers in structured logging mode (GUI integrations).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Keep matching command events visible even in quiet mode.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-print-files\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Print the watched file list at startup; --watch-print-files=false disables it.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-ignore <glob>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Ignore files matching glob (repeatable).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-include <glob>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Only watch files matching glob (repeatable). Empty means include all.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-auto-restart\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Restart on crashes; --watch-auto-restart=false disables a manifest setting.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-restart-delay <sec>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Delay before restart. Default: 1.0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-restart-max <N>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Maximum restart attempts (0 = unlimited). Default: 0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-self <path>\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Explicit path to fpm-watch executable (advanced).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  --watch-once\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"      Initialize (and optionally run once) then exit. Good for CI.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"CONFIGURATION (fpm.toml)\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  [extra.fpm-watch]  (same names as flags, without the --watch- prefix)\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  poll         = 0.5\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  debounce     = 0.2\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  rescan       = 0.0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  run-on-start = true\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  silent-fpm   = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  print-files  = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  deps         = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  auto-restart = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  restart-delay= 1.0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  restart-max  = 0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  self         = \"\"\"\"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  debug        = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  verbosity    = 0\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) '  log-format   = \"text\"' write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) '  fpm-executable = \"fpm\"' write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  output-markers = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  ignore       = []\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  include      = []\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  once         = false\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"EXAMPLES\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch build\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch test\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch --watch-deps test -- --list\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch --watch-auto-restart test\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"NOTES\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  fpm-watch ignores build/ to avoid infinite rebuild loops.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  Enable deps only if you want dependency source changes to trigger runs.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  Polling, debounce, and restart delays always use OS sleep to minimize idle CPU usage.\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"  To quit, press Ctrl+C (or create an empty file named .fpm-watch.stop).\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" end subroutine usage_print_only","tags":"","url":"proc/usage_print_only.html"},{"title":"validate_response_records – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine validate_response_records(path, has_options, error) Reject procedural response records before any M_CLI2 expansion occurs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path logical, intent(out) :: has_options type(error_t), intent(out), allocatable :: error Calls proc~~validate_response_records~~CallsGraph proc~validate_response_records validate_response_records fatal_error fatal_error proc~validate_response_records->fatal_error getline getline proc~validate_response_records->getline lower lower proc~validate_response_records->lower proc~starts_with starts_with proc~validate_response_records->proc~starts_with split split proc~validate_response_records->split Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~validate_response_records~~CalledByGraph proc~validate_response_records validate_response_records proc~prepare_response_options prepare_response_options proc~prepare_response_options->proc~validate_response_records proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~prepare_response_options proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine validate_response_records ( path , has_options , error ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path logical , intent ( out ) :: has_options type ( error_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: error character ( len = :), allocatable :: line , words (:), record integer :: unit , status has_options = . false . open ( newunit = unit , file = path , status = \"old\" , action = \"read\" , iostat = status ) if ( status /= 0 ) then call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot read response file \" // path ) return end if do call getline ( unit , line , iostat = status ) if ( status /= 0 ) exit if ( len_trim ( line ) > 4096 ) then call fatal_error ( error , \"Response record exceeds M_CLI2's 4096-byte limit: \" // path ) exit end if call split ( line , words , delimiters = \" \" // achar ( 9 ) // achar ( 13 )) if ( size ( words ) == 0 ) cycle record = lower ( trim ( words ( 1 ))) if ( starts_with ( record , \"#\" ) . or . starts_with ( record , \"@\" )) cycle select case ( record ) case ( \"options\" , \"option\" , \"-\" ) has_options = . true . case ( \"comment\" ) cycle case default call fatal_error ( error , \"Response file \" // path // \" contains unsupported record \" // record // & \"; fpm-watch accepts options/comments/OS sections, without system, print, or stop directives.\" ) exit end select end do close ( unit ) if ( status > 0 . and . . not . allocated ( error )) call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot read response file \" // path ) end subroutine validate_response_records","tags":"","url":"proc/validate_response_records.html"},{"title":"is_ignored_path – fpm-watch","text":"public pure function is_ignored_path(path, build_dir) result(ignored) Test normalized paths against a build directory or its slash-delimited fragments. Matches the directory itself, its descendants, and interior/trailing path\nfragments. An empty build directory matches nothing; dependency exceptions\nare applied by the graph collector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path character(len=*), intent(in) :: build_dir Return Value logical Calls proc~~is_ignored_path~~CallsGraph proc~is_ignored_path is_ignored_path proc~contains_path_fragment contains_path_fragment proc~is_ignored_path->proc~contains_path_fragment proc~normalize_path normalize_path proc~is_ignored_path->proc~normalize_path proc~starts_with starts_with proc~is_ignored_path->proc~starts_with proc~ends_with ends_with proc~contains_path_fragment->proc~ends_with Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~is_ignored_path~~CalledByGraph proc~is_ignored_path is_ignored_path proc~collection_add file_collection_t%collection_add proc~collection_add->proc~is_ignored_path proc~collect_manifest_metadata collect_manifest_metadata proc~collect_manifest_metadata->proc~collection_add proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings compute_watch_files_from_settings proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~collection_add proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~collect_manifest_metadata proc~gather_files_with_mask gather_files_with_mask proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~gather_files_with_mask proc~gather_include_closure gather_include_closure proc~gather_include_closure->proc~collection_add proc~gather_include_candidates gather_include_candidates proc~gather_include_closure->proc~gather_include_candidates proc~gather_files_with_mask->proc~gather_include_closure proc~gather_include_candidates->proc~gather_include_closure proc~run_graph_worker run_graph_worker proc~run_graph_worker->proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure logical function is_ignored_path ( path , build_dir ) result ( ignored ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path , build_dir character ( len = :), allocatable :: p , b p = normalize_path ( path ) b = normalize_path ( build_dir ) ignored = . false . if ( len_trim ( b ) == 0 ) return if ( p == b ) then ignored = . true . return end if if ( starts_with ( p , b // \"/\" )) then ignored = . true . return end if if ( contains_path_fragment ( p , b )) then ignored = . true . return end if end function is_ignored_path","tags":"","url":"proc/is_ignored_path.html"},{"title":"normalize_path – fpm-watch","text":"public pure function normalize_path(path) result(p) Right-trim a path, replace backslashes, and remove repeated leading ./ . Preserve case, interior separators, and .. segments; no filesystem lookup\nor canonicalization is performed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~normalize_path~~CalledByGraph proc~normalize_path normalize_path proc~collection_add file_collection_t%collection_add proc~collection_add->proc~normalize_path proc~is_ignored_path is_ignored_path proc~collection_add->proc~is_ignored_path proc~is_in_dep_dirs is_in_dep_dirs proc~collection_add->proc~is_in_dep_dirs proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings compute_watch_files_from_settings proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~normalize_path proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~collection_add proc~filter_watch_files filter_watch_files proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~filter_watch_files proc~collect_manifest_metadata collect_manifest_metadata proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~