ok = ( s ( n - ns + 1 : n ) == suffix ( 1 : ns )) end if end function ends_with","tags":"","url":"proc/ends_with.html"},{"title":"filter_watch_files – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine filter_watch_files(files, include, ignore, masks, preserve) Filter normalized paths and optional aligned masks, preserving order. Empty/unallocated include lists admit all files; matching ignore globs\nremove included paths. Manifests and optional marked metadata bypass both filters.\nAn unallocated file list is left unchanged. If masks are supplied but\nunallocated, create zero masks before filtering them with the files. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(string_t), intent(inout), allocatable :: files (:) Normalized input paths, replaced with the retained subset in the same order. type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: include (:) Include and ignore glob lists, respectively; empty/unallocated lists impose no restriction. type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: ignore (:) Include and ignore glob lists, respectively; empty/unallocated lists impose no restriction. integer(kind=int64), intent(inout), optional, allocatable :: masks (:) Aligned file masks; created as zeros if supplied but unallocated, then filtered with files. logical, intent(in), optional :: preserve (:) Aligned metadata markers; true entries bypass include/ignore filters. Calls proc~~filter_watch_files~~CallsGraph proc~filter_watch_files filter_watch_files basename basename proc~filter_watch_files->basename glob glob proc~filter_watch_files->glob proc~normalize_path normalize_path proc~filter_watch_files->proc~normalize_path Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~filter_watch_files~~CalledByGraph proc~filter_watch_files filter_watch_files proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings compute_watch_files_from_settings proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings->proc~filter_watch_files proc~run_graph_worker run_graph_worker proc~run_graph_worker->proc~compute_watch_files_from_settings Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine filter_watch_files ( files , include , ignore , masks , preserve ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: files (:) !! Normalized input paths, replaced with the retained subset in the same order. type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: include (:), ignore (:) !! Include and ignore glob lists, respectively; empty/unallocated lists impose no restriction. integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ), optional :: masks (:) !! Aligned file masks; created as zeros if supplied but unallocated, then filtered with files. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: preserve (:) !! Aligned metadata markers; true entries bypass include/ignore filters. logical , allocatable :: keep (:) type ( string_t ), allocatable :: out (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: outm (:) integer :: i , k , n , m if (. not . allocated ( files )) return n = size ( files ) allocate ( keep ( n )) do i = 1 , n keep ( i ) = should_keep ( files ( i )% s , include , ignore ) if ( present ( preserve )) keep ( i ) = keep ( i ) . or . preserve ( i ) end do m = count ( keep ) allocate ( out ( m )) if ( present ( masks )) then if (. not . allocated ( masks )) then allocate ( masks ( n )) masks = 0_int64 end if allocate ( outm ( m )) end if k = 0 do i = 1 , n if (. not . keep ( i )) cycle k = k + 1 out ( k )% s = files ( i )% s if ( present ( masks )) outm ( k ) = masks ( i ) end do call move_alloc ( out , files ) if ( present ( masks )) call move_alloc ( outm , masks ) deallocate ( keep ) contains !> Retain manifests unconditionally; otherwise require inclusion and no ignore match. logical function should_keep ( path , include_pats , ignore_pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: include_pats (:), ignore_pats (:) character ( len = :), allocatable :: b b = basename ( trim ( path )) if ( b == \"fpm.toml\" ) then ok = . true . return end if ok = match_include ( path , include_pats ) . and . (. not . match_any ( path , ignore_pats )) end function should_keep !> Test fpm globs after normalizing each nonempty pattern; an absent list matches nothing. logical function match_any ( path , pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: pats (:) integer :: j character ( len = :), allocatable :: pat ok = . false . if (. not . allocated ( pats )) return do j = 1 , size ( pats ) if ( len_trim ( pats ( j )% s ) == 0 ) cycle pat = normalize_path ( trim ( pats ( j )% s )) if ( glob ( trim ( path ), pat )) then ok = . true . return end if end do end function match_any !> Admit every path for an empty/unallocated include list; otherwise require a glob match. logical function match_include ( path , pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: pats (:) if (. not . allocated ( pats )) then ok = . true . return end if if ( size ( pats ) == 0 ) then ok = . true . return end if ok = match_any ( path , pats ) end function match_include end subroutine filter_watch_files","tags":"","url":"proc/filter_watch_files.html"},{"title":"inject_names_into_cmd – fpm-watch","text":"public  function inject_names_into_cmd(prefix, rest, names, windows) result(out) Insert already serialized names after fpm options and before a -- token. prefix includes the executable/subcommand; rest retains forwarded args. names must already contain quoted argv tokens. Optional windows selects\ndelimiter parsing rules. An empty prefix returns an empty string; empty\nnames simply rejoin prefix and rest. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: prefix Prefix up to and including the subcommand. character(len=*), intent(in) :: rest Remaining arguments after the subcommand. character(len=*), intent(in) :: names Space-separated names to inject. logical, intent(in), optional :: windows Explicit platform selection supports portable serialization checks. Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~inject_names_into_cmd~~CallsGraph proc~inject_names_into_cmd inject_names_into_cmd proc~is_windows is_windows proc~inject_names_into_cmd->proc~is_windows get_os_type get_os_type proc~is_windows->get_os_type Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement