ace to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine preserve_fingerprints ( old_files , old_fp , new_files , new_fp ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_files (:), new_files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_fp (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: new_fp (:) integer , allocatable :: old_order (:), new_order (:), scratch (:) integer :: nold , nnew , i , j logical :: aligned if (. not . allocated ( old_files )) return if (. not . allocated ( new_files )) return if (. not . allocated ( old_fp )) return if (. not . allocated ( new_fp )) return nold = size ( old_files ) nnew = size ( new_files ) if ( nold == 0 . or . nnew == 0 ) return if ( size ( old_fp ) /= nold . or . size ( new_fp ) /= nnew ) return aligned = nold == nnew if ( aligned ) then do i = 1 , nnew if ( old_files ( i )% s == new_files ( i )% s ) cycle aligned = . false . exit end do end if if ( aligned ) then new_fp = old_fp return end if allocate ( old_order ( nold ), new_order ( nnew ), scratch ( max ( nold , nnew ))) old_order = [( i , i = 1 , nold )] new_order = [( i , i = 1 , nnew )] call sort_path_indices ( old_files , old_order , scratch , 1 , nold ) call sort_path_indices ( new_files , new_order , scratch , 1 , nnew ) i = 1 j = 1 do while ( i <= nold . and . j <= nnew ) if ( old_files ( old_order ( i ))% s < new_files ( new_order ( j ))% s ) then i = i + 1 else if ( old_files ( old_order ( i ))% s > new_files ( new_order ( j ))% s ) then j = j + 1 else new_fp ( new_order ( j )) = old_fp ( old_order ( i )) i = i + 1 j = j + 1 end if end do end subroutine preserve_fingerprints","tags":"","url":"proc/preserve_fingerprints.html"},{"title":"scan_changes – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine scan_changes(files, fp_prev, fp_now, changed_idx, changed_count) Hash files and return 1-based indices differing from the accepted baseline. fp_prev , fp_now , and changed_idx must have space for every file.\nOnly changed_idx(:changed_count) is defined by this scan; fp_prev remains unchanged. An empty/unallocated file list reports no changes. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: files (:) integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: fp_prev (:) integer(kind=int64), intent(inout) :: fp_now (:) integer, intent(inout) :: changed_idx (:) integer, intent(out) :: changed_count Calls proc~~scan_changes~~CallsGraph proc~scan_changes scan_changes proc~file_fingerprint file_fingerprint proc~scan_changes->proc~file_fingerprint proc~fnv1a_mix_i64 fnv1a_mix_i64 proc~file_fingerprint->proc~fnv1a_mix_i64 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~scan_changes~~CalledByGraph proc~scan_changes scan_changes proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~scan_changes Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows