suppresses both output streams and takes precedence over stderr ,\nwhich redirects command stdout to stderr. Both options default to false.\nLaunch/wait errors log command.launch_failed and return 127; ordinary\nfailures preserve the child status. Optional interrupted reports this\ncommand's handled interruption, while termination_requested remains latched. POSIX uses a managed process group and a foreground monitor around /bin/sh .\nHUP/INT/QUIT/TERM reach the group, including nested supervisors; cancellation\nescalates after one second. Terminal ownership is restored after execution.\nWindows launches executables directly and safely encodes batch-script argv.\nConsole cancellation terminates its job. Normal exits retain background children. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: cmd Serialized command; caller is responsible for quoting individual argv tokens. integer, intent(out) :: exitstat Child/interrupt status, or 127 with a launch-failure event for OS execution errors. logical, intent(out), optional :: interrupted True if the wrapper handled a user interrupt during this command. logical, intent(in), optional :: silent Suppress both command output streams (default false); takes precedence over stderr. logical, intent(in), optional :: stderr Redirect command stdout to stderr (default false). logical, intent(in), optional :: inherit_workspace Keep supervisor workspace ownership for internal watcher/graph launches (default true).\nExternal commands clear that internal setting so surviving descendants own their workspaces. Calls proc~~execute_command~~CallsGraph proc~execute_command execute_command get_env get_env proc~execute_command->get_env interface~fpm_watch_execute fpm_watch_execute proc~execute_command->interface~fpm_watch_execute interface~log_int log_int proc~execute_command->interface~log_int proc~is_windows is_windows proc~execute_command->proc~is_windows proc~log_event log_event proc~execute_command->proc~log_eve