dges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine set_temp_directory ( path , error ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( error_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: error integer ( c_int ) :: status character ( len = 32 ) :: code status = fpm_watch_set_temp_directory ( path // c_null_char ) if ( status /= 0_c_int ) then write ( code , \"(i0)\" ) status call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot select graph workspace (OS error \" // trim ( code ) // \"): \" // path ) end if end subroutine set_temp_directory","tags":"","url":"proc/set_temp_directory.html"},{"title":"set_workspace_root – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine set_workspace_root(path, error, defined) Nest descendant workspaces under an owner that survives forced child termination. This internal setting leaves the user's native temporary-directory variables\nunchanged. Restore the inherited value after each supervised execution. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path type(error_t), intent(out), allocatable :: error logical, intent(in), optional :: defined Explicit presence preserves a previously defined empty environment value. Calls proc~~set_workspace_root~~CallsGraph proc~set_workspace_root set_workspace_root fatal_error fatal_error proc~set_workspace_root->fatal_error interface~fpm_watch_set_workspace_root fpm_watch_set_workspace_root proc~set_workspace_root->interface~fpm_watch_set_workspace_root Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~set_workspace_root~~CalledByGraph proc~set_workspace_root set_workspace_root proc~execute_command execute_command proc~execute_command->proc~set_workspace_root proc~execute_supervised_child execute_supervised_child proc~execute_supervised_child->proc~set_workspace_root proc~execute_supervised_child->proc~execute_command proc~compute_watch_snapshot compute_watch_snapshot proc~compute_watch_snapshot->proc~execute_command proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_command_and_report->proc~execute_command proc~supervisor_loop supervisor_loop proc~supervisor_loop->proc~execute_supervised_child proc~maybe_supervise maybe_supervise proc~maybe_supervise->proc~supervisor_loop proc~rebuild_watch_list rebuild_watch_list proc~rebuild_watch_list->proc~compute_watch_snapshot proc~run_once run_once proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~run_once proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~watcher_init->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~watcher_run->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplement