from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Stream complete file contents and compare watch-list snapshots. !! !! Every byte contributes to the fingerprint. Missing, empty, and unreadable files !! have distinct states; nonempty content uses a 63-bit hash. Hash collisions are !! still possible, so fingerprints are change detectors, not content identities. !! File reads share a reusable buffer and are intended for serial use. module watch_fingerprint use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : int64 use fpm_strings , only : string_t use fpm_filesystem , only : basename use fpm_command_line , only : fpm_build_settings implicit none private public init_fingerprints , scan_changes , accept_changes , manifest_key_from_files , file_fingerprint , watch_state_changed public preserve_fingerprints integer ( int64 ), parameter :: FNV_OFFSET = 1469598103934665603_int64 integer ( int64 ), parameter :: MASK32 = 4294967295_int64 integer , parameter :: BLOCK_SIZE = 65536 integer ( int64 ), parameter :: FILE_MISSING = 0_int64 , FILE_EMPTY = 1_int64 , FILE_UNREADABLE = 2_int64 !> Shared bounded scratch buffer; file fingerprinting is not reentrant. character ( len = BLOCK_SIZE ), save :: io_buf contains !> Compare unique path/fingerprint snapshots independently of file ordering. !! !! Unallocated path lists count as empty. Added/removed paths, changed !! fingerprints, or missing/mismatched fingerprint arrays for nonempty lists !! report a change. Two empty snapshots compare equal. Matching path order !! compares in linear time; reordered lists use sorted indices in O(n log n). pure logical function watch_state_changed ( old_files , old_fp , new_files , new_fp ) result ( changed ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_files (:), new_files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_fp (:), new_fp (:) integer :: nold , nnew , i integer , allocatable :: old_order (:), new_order (:), scratch (:) logical :: aligned nold = 0 nnew = 0 if ( allocated ( old_files )) nold = size ( old_files ) if ( allocated ( new_files )) nnew = size ( new_files ) changed = ( nold /= nnew ) if ( changed . or . nnew == 0 ) return changed = . true . if (. not . allocated ( old_fp )) return if (. not . allocated ( new_fp )) return if ( size ( old_fp ) /= nold . or . size ( new_fp ) /= nnew ) return aligned = . true . do i = 1 , nnew if ( old_files ( i )% s == new_files ( i )% s ) cycle aligned = . false . exit end do if ( aligned ) then changed = any ( old_fp /= new_fp ) return end if allocate ( old_order ( nold ), new_order ( nnew ), scratch ( nnew )) old_order = [( i , i = 1 , nold )] new_order = old_order call sort_path_indices ( old_files , old_order , scratch , 1 , nold ) call sort_path_indices ( new_files , new_order , scratch , 1 , nnew ) do i = 1 , nnew if ( old_files ( old_order ( i ))% s /= new_files ( new_order ( i ))% s ) return if ( old_fp ( old_order ( i )) /= new_fp ( new_order ( i ))) return end do changed = . false . end function watch_state_changed !> Preserve accepted baselines by path while retaining initial values for new paths. !! !! Both snapshots contain unique paths. Missing or malformed fingerprint arrays !! leave the new baseline unchanged. File ordering and membership may differ; !! matching order copies directly, otherwise sorted indices support a linear merge. pure subroutine preserve_fingerprints ( old_files , old_fp , new_files , new_fp ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_files (:), new_files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: old_fp (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: new_fp (:) integer , allocatable :: old_order (:), new_order (:), scratch (:) integer :: nold , nnew , i , j logical :: aligned if (. not . allocated ( old_files )) return if (. not . allocated ( new_files )) return if (. not . allocated ( old_fp )) return if (. not . allocated ( new_fp )) return nold = size ( old_files ) nnew = size ( new_files ) if ( nold == 0 . or . nnew == 0 ) return if ( size ( old_fp ) /= nold . or . size ( new_fp ) /= nnew ) return aligned = nold == nnew if ( aligned ) then do i = 1 , nnew if ( old_files ( i )% s == new_files ( i )% s ) cycle aligned = . false . exit end do end if if ( aligned ) then new_fp = old_fp return end if allocate ( old_order ( nold ), new_order ( nnew ), scratch ( max ( nold , nnew ))) old_order = [( i , i = 1 , nold )] new_order = [( i , i = 1 , nnew )] call sort_path_indices ( old_files , old_order , scratch , 1 , nold ) call sort_path_indices ( new_files , new_order , scratch , 1 , nnew ) i = 1 j = 1 do while ( i <= nold . and . j <= nnew ) if ( old_files ( old_order ( i ))% s < new_files ( new_order ( j ))% s ) then i = i + 1 else if ( old_files ( old_order ( i ))% s > new_files ( new_order ( j ))% s ) then j = j + 1 else new_fp ( new_order ( j )) = old_fp ( old_order ( i )) i = i + 1 j = j + 1 end if end do end subroutine preserve_fingerprints !> Stable merge sort of path indices; the file storage itself remains unchanged. pure recursive subroutine sort_path_indices ( files , order , scratch , first , last ) type ( string_t ), intent ( in ) :: files (:) integer , intent ( inout ) :: order (:), scratch (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: first , last integer :: middle , left , right , out if ( first >= last ) return middle = first + ( last - first ) / 2 call sort_path_indices ( files , order , scratch , first , middle ) call sort_path_indices ( files , order , scratch , middle + 1 , last ) left = first right = middle + 1 do out = first , last if ( left > middle ) then scratch ( out ) = order ( right ) right = right + 1 else if ( right > last ) then scratch ( out ) = order ( left ) left = left + 1 else if ( files ( order ( left ))% s <= files ( order ( right ))% s ) then scratch ( out ) = order ( left ) left = left + 1 else scratch ( out ) = order ( right ) right = right + 1 end if end do order ( first : last ) = scratch ( first : last ) end subroutine sort_path_indices !> Initialize fingerprint arrays for a watch list. !! !! Allocates `fp_prev`, `fp_now`, and `changed_idx` to match the size of !! `files`. Initial fingerprints are computed once and copied into `fp_now`. subroutine init_fingerprints ( files , fp_prev , fp_now , changed_idx ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: fp_prev (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: fp_now (:) integer , allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: changed_idx (:) integer :: n , i if (. not . allocated ( files )) then if ( allocated ( fp_prev )) deallocate ( fp_prev ) if ( allocated ( fp_now )) deallocate ( fp_now ) if ( allocated ( changed_idx )) deallocate ( changed_idx ) allocate ( fp_prev ( 0 ), fp_now ( 0 ), changed_idx ( 0 )) return end if n = size ( files ) if ( allocated ( fp_prev )) deallocate ( fp_prev ) if ( allocated ( fp_now )) deallocate ( fp_now ) if ( allocated ( changed_idx )) deallocate ( changed_idx ) allocate ( fp_prev ( n ), fp_now ( n ), changed_idx ( n )) do i = 1 , n fp_prev ( i ) = file_fingerprint ( files ( i )% s ) end do fp_now = fp_prev end subroutine init_fingerprints !> Hash files and return 1-based indices differing from the accepted baseline. !! !! `fp_prev`, `fp_now`, and `changed_idx` must have space for every file. !! Only `changed_idx(:changed_count)` is defined by this scan; `fp_prev` !! remains unchanged. An empty/unallocated file list reports no changes. subroutine scan_changes ( files , fp_prev , fp_now , changed_idx , changed_count ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: files (:) integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: fp_prev (:) integer ( int64 ), intent ( inout ) :: fp_now (:) integer , intent ( inout ) :: changed_idx (:) integer , intent ( out ) :: changed_count integer :: i , n changed_count = 0 if (. not . allocated ( files )) return n = size ( files ) if ( n == 0 ) return do i = 1 , n fp_now ( i ) = file_fingerprint ( files ( i )% s ) if ( fp_now ( i ) /= fp_prev ( i )) then changed_count = changed_count + 1 changed_idx ( changed_count ) = i end if end do end subroutine scan_changes !> Copy computed fingerprints into the baseline for valid changed indices. !! !! The engine accepts detected edits before graph refresh and command execution. !! Surviving paths retain those baselines through every refresh, so later edits !! remain detectable even while commands run. Invalid indices are skipped; !! both fingerprint arrays must be aligned. subroutine accept_changes ( fp_prev , fp_now , changed_idx , changed_count ) integer ( int64 ), intent ( inout ) :: fp_prev (:) integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: fp_now (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: changed_idx (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: changed_count integer :: j , i do j = 1 , changed_count i = changed_idx ( j ) if ( i >= 1 . and . i <= size ( fp_prev )) fp_prev ( i ) = fp_now ( i ) end do end subroutine accept_changes !> Mix selected fpm settings and watched manifest paths/fingerprints into a key. !! !! Includes build directory, toolchain, profile, compile/link flags, pruning, !! build-tests, and fpm features. File and feature ordering affects the key. !! The engine includes this key in refresh diagnostics; watched file changes !! trigger graph refreshes independently of the key. integer ( int64 ) function manifest_key_from_files ( settings , files ) result ( k ) class ( fpm_build_settings ), intent ( in ) :: settings type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: files (:) integer :: i character ( len = :), allocatable :: b k = FNV_OFFSET call mix_alloc ( k , settings % build_dir ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % compiler ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % c_compiler ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % cxx_compiler ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % archiver ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % profile ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % flag ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % cflag ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % cxxflag ) call mix_alloc ( k , settings % ldflag ) if ( settings % prune ) then call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , \"prune=1\" ) else call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , \"prune=0\" ) end if if ( settings % build_tests ) then call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , \"build_tests=1\" ) else call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , \"build_tests=0\" ) end if if ( allocated ( settings % features )) then do i = 1 , size ( settings % features ) call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , trim ( settings % features ( i )% s )) end do end if if (. not . allocated ( files )) return do i = 1 , size ( files ) b = basename ( files ( i )% s ) if ( b == \"fpm.toml\" ) then call fnv1a_mix_str ( k , files ( i )% s ) call fnv1a_mix_i64 ( k , file_fingerprint ( files ( i )% s )) end if end do contains !> Mix a right-trimmed, allocated, nonempty string into the current hash state. pure subroutine mix_alloc ( h , s ) integer ( int64 ), intent ( inout ) :: h character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: s if (. not . allocated ( s )) return if ( len_trim ( s ) == 0 ) return call fnv1a_mix_str ( h , trim ( s )) end subroutine mix_alloc end function manifest_key_from_files !> Hash every byte using bounded reads, reserving distinct non-content states. !! !! Missing files return zero, empty files one, and inquiry/open/read failures !! two. Successful nonempty hashes are negative and cannot equal those states. !! A size change during reading is treated as unreadable until the next poll. integer ( int64 ) function file_fingerprint ( path ) result ( fp ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path logical :: ex integer ( int64 ) :: sz , final_size , remaining , h integer :: u , ios , n , i fp = FILE_UNREADABLE inquire ( file = trim ( path ), exist = ex , iostat = ios ) if ( ios /= 0 ) return if (. not . ex ) then fp = FILE_MISSING return end if open ( newunit = u , file = trim ( path ), access = \"stream\" , form = \"unformatted\" , action = \"read\" , status = \"old\" , iostat = ios ) if ( ios /= 0 ) return sz = - 1_int64 inquire ( unit = u , size = sz , iostat = ios ) if ( ios /= 0 . or . sz < 0_int64 ) then close ( u ) return end if remaining = sz h = FNV_OFFSET do while ( remaining > 0_int64 ) n = int ( min ( remaining , int ( BLOCK_SIZE , int64 ))) read ( u , iostat = ios ) io_buf (: n ) if ( ios /= 0 ) exit do i = 1 , n call fnv1a_mix_i64 ( h , int ( iachar ( io_buf ( i : i )), int64 )) end do remaining = remaining - int ( n , int64 ) end do if ( remaining == 0_int64 ) then inquire ( unit = u , size = final_size , iostat = ios ) if ( ios == 0 ) then if ( final_size == sz ) then fp = ibset ( h , bit_size ( h ) - 1 ) if ( sz == 0_int64 ) fp = FILE_EMPTY end if end if end if close ( u ) end function file_fingerprint !> Mix each byte of a right-trimmed string using XOR and the FNV prime. pure subroutine fnv1a_mix_str ( h , s ) integer ( int64 ), intent ( inout ) :: h character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s integer :: i do i = 1 , len_trim ( s ) call fnv1a_mix_i64 ( h , int ( iachar ( s ( i : i )), int64 )) end do end subroutine fnv1a_mix_str !> Mix with the FNV prime modulo 2**64 using bounded 32-bit limbs. !! !! The prime is 2**40 + 435. Limb products fit signed int64, avoiding !! undefined signed overflow while preserving the intended bit pattern. pure subroutine fnv1a_mix_i64 ( h , x ) integer ( int64 ), intent ( inout ) :: h integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: x integer ( int64 ) :: low , high , product h = ieor ( h , x ) low = iand ( h , MASK32 ) high = iand ( shiftr ( h , 32 ), MASK32 ) product = low * 435_int64 high = high * 435_int64 + low * 256_int64 + shiftr ( product , 32 ) h = ior ( shiftl ( iand ( high , MASK32 ), 32 ), iand ( product , MASK32 )) end subroutine fnv1a_mix_i64 end module watch_fingerprint","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_fingerprint.f90.html"},{"title":"watch_cmdline.f90 – fpm-watch","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~watch_cmdline.f90~~EfferentGraph sou