s Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Read argv tokens, parse option values, and serialize command arguments. !! !! `quote_arg` always quotes the full token, including empty arguments. POSIX !! serialization uses single quotes; Windows uses double quotes and C-runtime !! backslash rules. Platform selection comes from `watch_platform:is_windows` !! unless a quoting caller supplies an explicit override. module watch_cmdline use , intrinsic :: ieee_arithmetic , only : ieee_is_finite use watch_util , only : starts_with use watch_platform , only : is_windows_os => is_windows implicit none private public get_arg , join_argv , parse_int , parse_real , quote_arg , is_windows_os , starts_with public watch_option_takes_value , parse_bool contains !> Parse trimmed, case-insensitive boolean spellings or return `default`. !! !! True accepts `1`, `true`, `on`, `yes`, `y`, `t`; false accepts `0`, `false`, !! `off`, `no`, `n`, `f`. Empty and unrecognized values use the fallback. pure logical function parse_bool ( s , default ) result ( v ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s logical , intent ( in ) :: default character ( len = :), allocatable :: t t = trim ( adjustl ( lower_ascii ( s ))) select case ( t ) case ( \"1\" , \"true\" , \"on\" , \"yes\" , \"y\" , \"t\" ) v = . true . case ( \"0\" , \"false\" , \"off\" , \"no\" , \"n\" , \"f\" ) v = . false . case default v = default end select end function parse_bool !> Normalize ASCII letters for case-insensitive option values. pure function lower_ascii ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = len ( s )) :: r integer :: k , c , da da = iachar ( \"a\" ) - iachar ( \"A\" ) do k = 1 , len ( s ) c = iachar ( s ( k : k )) if ( c >= iachar ( \"A\" ) . and . c <= iachar ( \"Z\" )) then r ( k : k ) = achar ( c + da ) else r ( k : k ) = s ( k : k ) end if end do end function lower_ascii !> Return whether a bare watcher option consumes the following argv token. pure logical function watch_option_takes_value ( a ) result ( takes_value ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: a select case ( a ) case ( \"--watch-restart-delay\" , \"--watch-restart-max\" , \"--watch-self\" , & \"--watch-rescan\" , \"--watch-ignore\" , \"--watch-include\" , & \"--watch-poll\" , \"--watch-debounce\" , \"--watch-log-format\" , \"--watch-fpm\" ) takes_value = . true . case default takes_value = . false . end select end function watch_option_takes_value !> Return argv entry `i`, or an empty string for a missing, empty, or unreadable argument. function get_arg ( i ) result ( a ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! Argument index: 0 is the executable name; actual arguments start at 1. character ( len = :), allocatable :: a integer :: n , istat n = 0 call get_command_argument ( i , length = n , status = istat ) if ( istat /= 0 . or . n <= 0 ) then a = \"\" return end if allocate ( character ( len = n ) :: a ) call get_command_argument ( i , value = a , status = istat ) if ( istat /= 0 ) a = \"\" end function get_arg !> Serialize argv entries from `i1` through `i2` with spaces and platform quoting. !! !! Every token, including an empty one, passes through `quote_arg`. A reversed !! range returns an empty command string. function join_argv ( i1 , i2 ) result ( s ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 !! Inclusive range of argv indices to join. character ( len = :), allocatable :: s character ( len = :), allocatable :: a integer :: i s = \"\" do i = i1 , i2 a = get_arg ( i ) if ( i > i1 ) s = s // \" \" s = s // quote_arg ( a ) end do end function join_argv !> Serialize one complete argv token, preserving whitespace and empty arguments. !! !! Optional `windows` overrides host detection. Windows doubles trailing !! backslashes and escapes embedded double quotes for the C-runtime parser. !! POSIX uses single quotes, breaking out of them to represent embedded quotes. function quote_arg ( a , windows ) result ( q ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: a logical , intent ( in ), optional :: windows !! Explicit platform selection supports portable serialization checks. character ( len = :), allocatable :: q logical :: use_windows if ( present ( windows )) then use_windows = windows else use_windows = is_windows_os () end if if ( use_windows ) then q = '\"' // escape_quotes_win ( a ) // '\"' else q = \"'\" // escape_quotes_sh ( a ) // \"'\" end if contains !> Escape embedded quotes and trailing backslashes for a double-quoted Windows argv token. pure function escape_quotes_win ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = :), allocatable :: r integer :: j , backslashes r = \"\" backslashes = 0 do j = 1 , len ( s ) if ( s ( j : j ) == achar ( 92 )) then backslashes = backslashes + 1 cycle end if if ( s ( j : j ) == '\"' ) then r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), 2 * backslashes + 1 ) // '\"' else r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), backslashes ) // s ( j : j ) end if backslashes = 0 end do r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), 2 * backslashes ) end function escape_quotes_win !> Replace embedded single quotes with quoted fragments suitable for a POSIX shell. pure function escape_quotes_sh ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = :), allocatable :: r integer :: j r = \"\" do j = 1 , len ( s ) if ( s ( j : j ) == \"'\" ) then r = r // \"'\"\"'\"\"'\" else r = r // s ( j : j ) end if end do end function escape_quotes_sh end function quote_arg !> Read an integer with list-directed input; return `default` if the read fails. pure integer function parse_int ( s , default ) result ( v ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s integer , intent ( in ) :: default integer :: ios v = default read ( s , * , iostat = ios ) v if ( ios /= 0 ) v = default end function parse_int !> Read a finite real; return `default` if the read fails or yields NaN/infinity. pure real function parse_real ( s , default ) result ( v ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s real , intent ( in ) :: default integer :: ios v = default read ( s , * , iostat = ios ) v if ( ios /= 0 ) v = default if (. not . ieee_is_finite ( v )) v = default end function parse_real end module watch_cmdline","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_cmdline.f90.html"},{"title":"watch_platform.f90 – fpm-watch","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~watch_platform.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90 watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_platform.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_types.f90 watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_util.f90 watch_util.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90->sourcefile~watch_util.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~watch_platform.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90 watch_cli.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90 watch_engine.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_cli.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90 watch_exec.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_exec.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90 watch_graph_worker.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90 watch_fpm_graph.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90 watch_restart.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Portable synchronous process execution and stdout redirection. !! !! C wrappers launch commands, forward user interrupts, and redirect raw fpm !! library output. An interrupt received while waiting for a command latches !! `stop_requested`; ordinary nonzero child exits do not. OS detection uses !! `fpm_environment:get_os_type`. module watch_platform use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_char , c_int , c_size_t , c_null_char use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : output_unit use watch_log , only : log_event , log_int , log_string use fpm_environment , only : get_os_type , OS_WINDOWS , get_env use fpm_error , only : error_t , fatal_error implicit none private public is_windows , execute_command , termination_requested public begin_raw_output , end_raw_output , create_temp_directory , remove_temp_directory , set_temp_directory public set_workspace_root !> Latched cancellation request; ordinary child exit codes do not set it. logical , save :: stop_requested = . false . interface !> C process wrapper returning child status or 127 for a launch/wait error. !! !! `command` is NUL-terminated. On Windows, `silent` selects inherited streams: !! 0 normal, 1 discard both outputs, 2 redirect stdout to stderr. POSIX ignores !! this mode because the Fortran wrapper appends shell redirections. !! `interrupted` reports handled user interrupts; `launch_error` holds the OS !! error code separately from ordinary child failure. function fpm_watch_execute ( command , silent , interrupted , launch_error ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_execute\" ) result ( status ) import c_char , c_int implicit none !> NUL-terminated command bytes interoperating with a C string. ! allow(C071) character ( kind = c_char ), intent ( in ) :: command ( * ) integer ( c_int ), value :: silent integer ( c_int ), intent ( out ) :: interrupted integer ( c_int ), intent ( out ) :: launch_error integer ( c_int ) :: status end function fpm_watch_execute !> Redirect descriptor 1 to stderr; return a saved stdout descriptor or a negative OS error. function fpm_watch_redirect_stdout () bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_redirect_stdout\" ) result ( saved ) import c_int implicit none integer ( c_int ) :: saved end function fpm_watch_redirect_stdout !> Restore and close a saved stdout descriptor; return zero on success or an OS error. function fpm_watch_restore_stdout ( saved ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_restore_stdout\" ) result ( error ) import c_int implicit none integer ( c_int ), value :: saved integer ( c_int ) :: error end function fpm_watch_restore_stdout !> Reserve a uniquely named private temporary directory; return an OS error or zero. function fpm_watch_create_temp_directory ( path , capacity ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_create_temp_directory\" ) result ( error ) import c_char , c_int , c_size_t implicit none !> The C helper writes at most the caller-provided capacity, including NUL. ! allow(C071, C072) character ( kind = c_char ), intent ( out ) :: path ( * ) integer ( c_size_t ), value :: capacity integer ( c_int ) :: error end function fpm_watch_create_temp_directory !> Remove a workspace without following links; a missing path is already clean. function fpm_watch_remove_temp_directory ( path ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_remove_temp_directory\" ) result ( error ) import c_char , c_int implicit none ! allow(C071) character ( kind = c_char ), intent ( in ) :: path ( * ) integer ( c_int ) :: error end function fpm_watch_remove_temp_directory !> Set all native temporary-directory variables inside a graph worker. function fpm_watch_set_temp_directory ( path ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_set_temp_directory\" ) result ( error ) import c_char , c_int implicit none ! allow(C071) character ( kind = c_char ), intent ( in ) :: path ( * ) integer ( c_int ) :: error end function fpm_watch_set_temp_directory !> Select an inherited supervisor workspace, or clear it with an empty path. function fpm_watch_set_workspace_root ( path , defined ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_set_workspace_root\" ) result ( error ) import c_char , c_int implicit none ! allow(C071) character ( kind = c_char ), intent ( in ) :: path ( * ) integer ( c_int ), value :: defined integer ( c_int ) :: error end function fpm_watch_set_workspace_root end interface contains !> Wait for a command and return its status while latching handled user interrupts. !! !! `silent` suppresses both output streams and takes precedence over `stderr`, !! which redirects command stdout to stderr. Both options default to false. !! Launch/wait errors log `command.launch_failed` and return 127; ordinary !! failures preserve the child status. Optional `interrupted` reports this !! command's handled interruption, while `termination_requested` remains latched. !! !! POSIX uses a managed process group and a foreground monitor around `/bin/sh`. !! HUP/INT/QUIT/TERM reach the group, including nested supervisors; cancellation !! escalates after one second. Terminal ownership is restored after execution. !! Windows launches executables directly and safely encodes batch-script argv. !! Console cancellation terminates its job. Normal exits retain background children. subroutine execute_command ( cmd , exitstat , interrupted , silent , stderr , inherit_workspace ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: cmd !! Serialized command; caller is responsible for quoting individual argv tokens. integer , intent ( out ) :: exitstat !! Child/interrupt status, or 127 with a launch-failure event for OS execution errors. logical , intent ( out ), optional :: interrupted !! True if the wrapper handled a user interrupt during this command. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: silent !! Suppress both command output streams (default false); takes precedence over stderr. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: stderr !! Redirect command stdout to stderr (default false). logical , intent ( in ), optional :: inherit_workspace !! Keep supervisor workspace ownership for internal watcher/graph launches (default true). !! External commands clear that internal setting so surviving descendants own their workspaces. integer ( c_int ) :: status , was_interrupted , launch_error , silent_mode character ( len = :), allocatable :: effective_cmd , inherited_root logical :: isolate_workspace , root_defined integer :: environment_status type ( error_t ), allocatable :: error , restore_error silent_mode = 0_c_int if ( present ( stderr )) then if ( stderr ) silent_mode = 2_c_int end if if ( present ( silent )) then if ( silent ) silent_mode = 1_c_int end if effective_cmd = trim ( cmd ) if (. not . is_windows ()) then if ( silent_mode == 1_c_int ) effective_cmd = effective_cmd // \" >/dev/null 2>&1\" if ( silent_mode == 2_c_int ) effective_cmd = effective_cmd // \" 1>&2\" end if isolate_workspace = . false . if ( present ( inherit_workspace )) isolate_workspace = . not . inherit_workspace if ( present ( interrupted )) interrupted = . false . if ( isolate_workspace ) then inherited_root = get_env ( \"FPM_WATCH_WORKSPACE_ROOT\" ) call get_environment_variable ( \"FPM_WATCH_WORKSPACE_ROOT\" , status = environment_status ) root_defined = environment_status == 0 call set_workspace_root ( \"\" , error ) if ( allocated ( error )) then call set_workspace_root ( inherited_root , restore_error , defined = root_defined ) call log_event ( \"error\" , \"command.workspace_failed\" , error % message ) exitstat = 127 return end if end if status = fpm_watch_execute ( effective_cmd // c_null_char , silent_mode , was_interrupted , launch_error ) stop_requested = stop_requested . or . was_interrupted /= 0_c_int if ( present ( interrupted )) interrupted = was_interrupted /= 0_c_int if ( isolate_workspace ) then call set_workspace_root ( inherited_root , error , defined = root_defined ) if ( allocated ( error )) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"command.workspace_failed\" , error % message ) exitstat = 127 return end if end if if ( launch_error /= 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"command.launch_failed\" , \"Cannot execute command: \" // trim ( cmd ), & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( launch_error )), log_string ( \"command\" , trim ( cmd ))]) exitstat = 127 else exitstat = int ( status ) end if end subroutine execute_command !> Optionally redirect process stdout to stderr, flushing Fortran output first. !! !! Return a saved C descriptor in `saved`, or -1 when redirection is disabled. !! Pair successful redirection with `end_raw_output`. Redirection failure logs !! an error and exits with status 127; this is process-wide, not thread-local. subroutine begin_raw_output ( redirect , saved ) logical , intent ( in ) :: redirect integer ( c_int ), intent ( out ) :: saved saved = - 1_c_int if (. not . redirect ) return flush ( output_unit ) saved = fpm_watch_redirect_stdout () if ( saved < 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"log.redirect_failed\" , \"Cannot redirect fpm output to stderr\" , & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( - saved ))]) stop 127 end if end subroutine begin_raw_output !> Flush raw library output, restore stdout, and close the saved C descriptor. !! !! Negative `saved` values are no-ops. Restoration failure logs an error and !! exits with status 127; a saved descriptor must only be restored once. subroutine end_raw_output ( saved ) integer ( c_int ), intent ( in ) :: saved integer ( c_int ) :: error if ( saved < 0_c_int ) return flush ( output_unit ) error = fpm_watch_restore_stdout ( saved ) if ( error /= 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"log.redirect_failed\" , \"Cannot restore stdout after fpm model operation\" , & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( error ))]) stop 127 end if end subroutine end_raw_output !> Reserve a private temporary directory and return its absolute path. !! !! POSIX permissions are restricted to its owner. Pair success with !! `remove_temp_directory`, including cancellation and failure paths. subroutine create_temp_directory ( path , error ) character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: path type ( error_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: error character ( kind = c_char ) :: buffer ( 32768 ) character ( len = 32 ) :: code integer ( c_int ) :: status integer :: i , n path = \"\" status = fpm_watch_create_temp_directory ( buffer , int ( size ( buffer ), c_size_t )) if ( status /= 0_c_int ) then write ( code , \"(i0)\" ) status call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot create watcher workspace (OS error \" // trim ( code ) // & \"); check the temporary directory and its permissions\" ) return end if n = 0 do i = 1 , size ( buffer ) if ( buffer ( i ) == c_null_char ) exit n = n + 1 end do path = repeat ( \" \" , n ) do i = 1 , n path ( i : i ) = buffer ( i ) end do end subroutine create_temp_directory !> Remove a workspace and its contents without following links, tolerating repeated cleanup. subroutine remove_temp_directory ( path ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path integer ( c_int ) :: status if ( len ( path ) == 0 ) return status = fpm_watch_remove_temp_directory ( path // c_null_char ) if ( status /= 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"warn\" , \"temp.cleanup_failed\" , \"Cannot remove watcher workspace: \" // path , & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( status )), log_string ( \"path\" , path )]) end if end subroutine remove_temp_directory !> Direct native temporary files into the worker's private workspace. !! !! Call only in the isolated worker; this updates process-wide TMPDIR/TMP/TEMP. subroutine set_temp_directory ( path , error ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( error_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: error integer ( c_int ) :: status character ( len = 32 ) :: code status = fpm_watch_set_temp_directory ( path // c_null_char ) if ( status /= 0_c_int ) then write ( code , \"(i0)\" ) status call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot select graph workspace (OS error \" // trim ( code ) // \"): \" // path ) end if end subroutine set_temp_directory !> Nest descendant workspaces under an owner that survives forced child termination. !! !! This internal setting leaves the user's native temporary-directory variables !! unchanged. Restore the inherited value after each supervised execution. subroutine set_workspace_root ( path , error , defined ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( error_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: error logical , intent ( in ), optional :: defined !! Explicit presence preserves a previously defined empty environment value. integer ( c_int ) :: status integer ( c_int ) :: present_value character ( len = 32 ) :: code present_value = merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , len ( path ) > 0 ) if ( present ( defined )) present_value = merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , defined ) status = fpm_watch_set_workspace_root ( path // c_null_char , present_value ) if ( status /= 0_c_int ) then write ( code , \"(i0)\" ) status call fatal_error ( error , \"Cannot select supervisor workspace (OS error \" // trim ( code ) // \"): \" // path ) end if end subroutine set_workspace_root !> Return the process-wide interruption flag latched by prior command executions. logical function termination_requested () result ( requested ) requested = stop_requested end function termination_requested !> Return whether the current OS is Windows. logical function is_windows () is_windows = ( get_os_type () == OS_WINDOWS ) end function is_windows end module watch_platform","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_platform.f90.html"},{"title":"watch_time.f90 – fpm-watch","text":"Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~watch_time.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~watch_time.f90 watch_time.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90 watch_engine.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_time.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90 watch_restart.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_time.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Use OS sleep for polling, debounce, and restart delays. !! !! Windows uses `Sleep`; POSIX uses `nanosleep`, retrying the remaining duration !! after EINTR. Waiting always yields to the scheduler and has no global mode. !! These waits do not poll the watcher's termination flag. module watch_time use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_double implicit none private public sleep_seconds !> Binding to the C implementation of portable OS sleep. interface !> C OS sleep; `sec` is passed by value, with nonpositive/nonfinite values ignored. subroutine fpm_watch_sleep_seconds ( sec ) bind ( C , name = \"fpm_watch_sleep_seconds\" ) import c_double implicit none real ( c_double ), value :: sec end subroutine fpm_watch_sleep_seconds end interface contains !> Wait approximately `s` seconds while yielding to the OS scheduler. !! !! Nonpositive/nonfinite values return immediately. The portable C shim !! handles platform limits and interrupted sleeps without busy waiting. subroutine sleep_seconds ( s ) real , intent ( in ) :: s call fpm_watch_sleep_seconds ( real ( s , c_double )) end subroutine sleep_seconds end module watch_time","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_time.f90.html"},{"title":"watch_types.f90 – fpm-watch","text":"Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~watch_types.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~watch_types.f90 watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_banner.f90 watch_banner.f90 sourcefile~watch_banner.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90 watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_banner.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90 watch_cli.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_config.f90 watch_config.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_config.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_cli.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_config.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90 watch_engine.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_banner.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_cli.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90 watch_exec.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_exec.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90 watch_graph_worker.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_engine.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_exec.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90 watch_fpm_graph.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_graph_worker.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90 watch_restart.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_platform.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Shared types used throughout `fpm-watch`. !! !! This module defines the configuration records used to pass options and !! `fpm` settings into the engine. module watch_types use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : int64 use fpm_strings , only : string_t use fpm_command_line , only : fpm_build_settings implicit none private public watch_opts_t , root_info_t , watch_config_t , watch_snapshot_t !> Watcher options assembled from defaults, manifest values, and leading CLI flags. !! !! Timing fields are seconds. `restart_count` identifies the child generation !! used in command cycle IDs. Watcher and supervisor share these parsed options. !! `set_watch_defaults` initializes format/executable strings and list arrays. type watch_opts_t !> Verbosity level: !! !! - `-1`: quiet (errors and enabled output protocol) !! - `0`: normal !! - `1..2`: more detail integer :: verbosity = 0 !> Output format: text (default), json (JSON Lines), or logfmt. character ( len = :), allocatable :: log_format !> Executable used for build/test/run; defaults to `fpm` on PATH. character ( len = :), allocatable :: fpm_executable !> Enable debug-level records; quiet mode still suppresses them. logical :: debug = . false . !> Seconds between polling scans; normalized to at least 0.05. real :: poll = 0.5 !> Seconds to wait after detecting a change before resampling. real :: debounce = 0.2 !> Optional periodic rescan interval (seconds). `0` disables periodic rescans. real :: rescan = 0.0 !> Run the command once immediately on startup. logical :: run_on_start = . true . !> Request a startup file list; the logger additionally requires verbosity 2. logical :: print_files_once = . false . !> Suppress both command output streams; watcher and model records remain separate. logical :: silent_fpm = . false . !> Bracket command stderr and force cycle events in structured logging only. logical :: output_markers = . false . !> Internal supervisor generation, retained during manifest refresh. integer :: restart_count = 0 !> Also watch dependency project sources (can include paths under build dir). logical :: watch_deps = . false . !> Ignore globs, applied after include rules; manifest/version metadata bypass filtering. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: ignore (:) !> Include globs; empty means all eligible files. Manifest/version metadata always remain. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: include (:) !> Run once (init + optional run-on-start) and exit (CI-friendly). logical :: once = . false . !> Restart failed watcher children until success or the configured limit. logical :: auto_restart = . false . !> Internal child marker preventing recursive supervision. logical :: is_child = . false . !> Seconds between failed child exits and the next launch. real :: restart_delay = 1.0 !> Maximum restarts after initial launch; zero means unlimited. integer :: restart_max = 0 !> Explicit supervisor child executable, otherwise resolved from argv/environment. character ( len = :), allocatable :: self_exe end type watch_opts_t !> Executable basename and one root bit used for affected-target selection. !! !! Graph construction assigns unique bits to up to 64 run/test roots; graphs outside !! that range return an empty root array and do not support name injection. type root_info_t !> Executable output basename without suffix, used as an fpm target pattern. character ( len = :), allocatable :: name !> Single bit identifying this root in target and file membership masks. integer ( int64 ) :: mask = 0_int64 end type root_info_t !> One aligned watch-list snapshot, including membership and change baselines. type watch_snapshot_t type ( string_t ), allocatable :: files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: file_mask (:) type ( root_info_t ), allocatable :: roots (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: fp_prev (:), fp_now (:) integer , allocatable :: changed_idx (:) end type watch_snapshot_t !> Fully assembled watcher configuration. !! !! This record is the primary input to `watcher_t%init()`. type watch_config_t !> Watcher options. type ( watch_opts_t ) :: w !> Absolute project directory shared by manifest/model/file resolution. character ( len = :), allocatable :: project_dir !> Absolute named response-file candidates, retained to detect edits or new overrides. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: response_files (:) !> Full command line string to execute (e.g., `fpm test -- ...`). character ( len = :), allocatable :: fpm_cmdline !> Selected `fpm` subcommand (`build`, `test`, or `run`). character ( len = :), allocatable :: subcmd !> Typed `fpm` settings corresponding to `subcmd`. class ( fpm_build_settings ), allocatable :: settings !> Cached prefix up to and including the subcommand token (for injection). character ( len = :), allocatable :: cmd_prefix !> Cached remainder after the subcommand token (for injection). character ( len = :), allocatable :: cmd_rest end type watch_config_t end module watch_types","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_types.f90.html"}]}